DESCRIPTION:The International Day for Tolerance falls on November 16\, and 
 it has two founding documents rather than one: UNESCO proclaimed the day i
 n 1995\, and the United Nations General Assembly invited member states to 
 observe it the year after. The date was not chosen at random. November 16 
 is the anniversary of UNESCO's own constitution\, adopted on that day in 1
 945\, and the declaration that created the observance was adopted exactly 
 fifty years later.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/international-da
 y-for-tolerance/
